# Trace / Graphic Performance Roadmap

Durable detail:
- Parent: `doc/Trace_Graphic_Performance_Plan.md`
- Trace redesign: `doc/Trace_Virtual_List_Redesign.md`

Update those docs when work lands. This rule tells agents **what to optimize next**.

## Product rule

Trace and Graphic are make-or-break. Trace T1–T5, Graphic Stage 2 (P1-1 / P1-3), and B6 are done.
Measurement ≠ UI: decode / filter / MinMax / LOD never in `paintEvent` / `replot`.

## Done (do not redo)

- Phase A/B (incl. B6 timer silence) + P0-1 LOD
- T0–T5 Trace redesign
- P1-1 Graphic: no per-view rawData twin for SampleStore-backed signals
- P1-3 Graphic: OverlaySelected default, skip hidden, per-signal dirty rebuild
- T5 / P1-4 visibility silence

## Next — measure, then P2 if needed

1. Manual acceptance under high load (Trace + Graphic together)
2. Only if still heavy: C1b custom Trace painter / C2 Graphic strip compositor / C3 LOD pyramid

## Agent behavior

- Prefer measurement + user-reported hotspots over drive-by refactors.
- English only in non-`.md` files (see `no-chinese-in-code`).
- After landing an item: mark it in `doc/Trace_Graphic_Performance_Plan.md` + Decision log.
